-- erwartet: N008
-- **The overlap boundary, to the exact bit.** `beispiele/gift/106` overlaps by two bits
-- (`@[7:4]` against `@[5:2]`); the comment there already names the touching case as clean
-- (`version @[7:4]` / `dscp @[7:2]` are two bytes). This is the edge between them: `a`
-- owns bit 4 and `b` claims it too, so the two ranges touch in exactly one shared bit and
-- `N008` must fire. A mask comparison off by one in either direction moves this file to
-- the wrong side -- silent, or refusing the clean touch beside it.
-- Measured 2026-09-11 against the unchanged checker: falls with `N008`.

module gift::bit_ranges_touch_by_one_bit {

format Kopf endian big {
    a : u8 @[7:4],
    b : u8 @[4:0],
}

}
